  "content": {
    "title": "Vanderbilt basketball defeats Illinois to make first Sweet 16 since 2009",
    "text": "Updated March 23, 2026, 9:10 p.m. CTVanderbilt women's basketball is heading to its first Sweet 16 since 2009.The No. 2 seed Commodores (29-4) pulled away from No. 7 Illinois in the fourth quarter of the March 23 matchup at Memorial Gymnasium to win their second-round game 75-57 and advance to a matchup with No. 6 seed Notre Dame on March 27 in Fort Worth, Texas.Mikayla Blakes set the NCAA Division I sophomore scoring record during the game as she nearly put up a triple-double with 25 points, 10 rebounds and nine assists. Justine Pissott scored 18 points and Aubrey Galvan had 12.Vanderbilt's defense held the Illini (22-12) to under 30% shooting from the field. Watch Vanderbilt vs Illinois live with Fubo (free trial)Vanderbilt vs Illinois score updates Vanderbilt vs Illinois score update: Commodores extend leadVanderbilt led, 66-47, with 6:13 to go in the fourth quarter as Mikayla Blakes is up to 22 points and Justine Pissott up to 18. Vanderbilt vs Illinois score update: Quick threes give Commodores breathing roomVanderbilt put up a quick 6-0 run over 30 seconds with 3-pointers from Mikayla Blakes and Aubrey Galvan. The Commodores are up, 52-37, with 3:41 in the third as Illinois called timeout. Vanderbilt vs Illinois score update: Illinois narrows thingsVanderbilt held a 45-35 lead at the third quarter media timeout with 4:58 to go in the third quarter. Illinois has narrowed the lead a bit. Vanderbilt vs Illinois score update: Commodores hold leadVanderbilt led, 31-19, at the media timeout of the second quarter with 4:23 to go in the period. Justine Pissott leads Vanderbilt with 10 points. Vanderbilt vs Illinois score update: Commodores end first quarter on runVanderbilt led, 21-8, at the end of the first quarter after ending the period on a 9-0 run. Illinois missed 14 straight shots to end the quarter and didn't score for the final 2:56. Vanderbilt vs Illinois score update: Sloppy start to the gameVanderbilt led, 8-6, at the first quarter media timeout with 4:54 left in the period. Vanderbilt got off to a 3-for-10 start from the field, while Illinois is 3-for-8. Vanderbilt vs Illinois starting lineupsVanderbiltG Aubrey GalvanG Mikayla BlakesG Ndjakalenga MwenentandaG Justine PissottF Sacha WashingtonIllinoisG Aaliyah GuytonG Destiny JacksonG Jasmine Brown-HaggerF Berry WallaceF Cearah ParchmentWhy Illinois' Berry Wallace is wearing mask vs Vanderbilt What time does Vanderbilt vs Illinois play today? Date: Monday, March 23Time: 6 p.m. CTLocation: Memorial GymnasiumWhat channel is Vanderbilt vs Illinois game on today? TV channel: ESPN2Streaming: Fubo (subscribe today)Radio: 94.9 The Fan and the Vanderbilt Athletics appVanderbilt vs Illinois prediction Vanderbilt 85, Illinois 79 Vanderbilt vs Illinois injury updates Vanderbilt will have its full roster available save Madison Greene, who is out for the season.Vanderbilt basketball first, second round schedule in NCAA tournamentSaturday, March 21Game 1: Vanderbilt 102, High Point 61Game 2: Illinois 66, Colorado 57Monday, March 23Vanderbilt vs Illinois, 6 p.m. CT (ESPN2)Aria Gerson covers Vanderbilt athletics for The Tennessean. Contact her at agerson@gannett.com or on X, formerly Twitter, @aria_gerson.We occasionally recommend interesting products and services. If you make a purchase by clicking one of the links, we may earn an affiliate fee. USA TODAY Network newsrooms operate independently, and this doesn’t influence our coverage.",
